      <h2 class="section-title">Important Change for 2003</h2>
      <p>Increased self-employed health insurance deduction. In 2003, the self-employed health insurance deduction increases from 70% to 75% of the cost of the insurance. For more information, see Health Insurance Costs of Self-Employed Members, later, under Income Tax: Income and Expenses.</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Important Reminder</h2>
      <p>Photographs of missing children. The Inter-national Center for Missing and Exploited Children (ICMEC) has a program that helps track missing children. You can help bring these children home by looking at the posters and calling 1-800-THE-LOST (1-800-843-5678) if you recognize a child.</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Introduction</h2>
      <p>Social security and Medicare taxes are collected from members of the clergy and religious workers. Under the Self-Employment Contributions Act (SECA), the self-employed person pays all the taxes. Under the Federal Insurance Contributions Act (FICA), the employer and the employee each pay half of the taxes. No earnings are subject to both systems.</p>
