  <h3 class="subsection-title">This publication covers the following topics</h3>
  <p>This publication covers the following topics about the collection of social security and Medicare taxes from members of the clergy and religious workers.</p>

  <h3 class="subsection-title">Which earnings are taxed under SECA and which under FICA?</h3>
  <p>Which earnings are taxed under SECA and which under FICA? (See Table 1 to determine whether FICA or SECA applies to your earnings.)</p>

  <h3 class="subsection-title">How a member of the clergy (minister, priest, etc.) is treated</h3>
  <p>How a member of the clergy (minister, priest, etc.) is treated for tax purposes. This includes how to figure out net earnings from self-employment tax.</p>

  <h3 class="subsection-title">This publication also covers certain income and expense deductions</h3>
  <p>This publication also covers certain income and expense deductions that are available to members of the clergy and religious workers. For more information, see <span data-field="section_ref">{{ section_ref }}</span>.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <p>Note. In this publication, the term <span data-field="term_definition">{{ term_definition }}</span> is used in its religious sense and not in the sense used in its secular sense.</p>
  </div>

  <h3 class="subsection-title">Comments and suggestions.</h3>
  <p>We welcome your comments about this publication and your suggestions for future editions.</p>

  <h3 class="subsection-title">Table 1. Are You Covered Under FICA or SECA?</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Occupation</th>
        <th>Covered under FICA?</th>
        <th>Covered under SECA?</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Christian Science practitioner or reader</td>
        <td>NO. You are exempt.*</td>
        <td>NO. You are exempt.*</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Member of a recognized religious sect</td>
        <td>YES, if you are an employee and do not have an approved exemption from the IRS.</td>
        <td>YES, if you are self-employed and do not have an approved exemption from the IRS.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Member of a religious order who has taken a vow of poverty</td>
        <td>NO. You are exempt.*</td>
        <td>NO. You are exempt.*</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Member of a religious order who has not taken a vow of poverty</td>
        <td>NO. If neither of the above applies.*</td>
        <td>NO. You are exempt.*</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Minister</td>
        <td>NO. You are exempt.</td>
        <td>NO. You are exempt.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Religious worker (church employee)</td>
        <td>NO, if your employer elected not to have you covered.</td>
        <td>YES, if your employer elected not to have you covered under FICA.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

