  <h2 class="section-title">Members of Recognized Religious Sects</h2>
  <p>If you are a member of a recognized religious sect, you may be exempt from social security and Medicare taxes. You must meet certain requirements to qualify for this exemption.</p>
  <p>If you are a member of a recognized religious sect, you must meet the following requirements:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>You must be a member of a recognized religious sect.</li>
    <li>You must meet the requirements of the sect.</li>
    <li>You must not be subject to SE tax or FICA tax.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="section-title">Exemption From FICA Taxes</h2>
  <p>Generally, under FICA, the employer and the employee pay half of the social security and Medicare taxes. However, certain individuals may be exempt from FICA taxes.</p>
  <p>If you are an employee of a church or religious organization, you may be exempt from FICA taxes. For more information, see <span data-field="section_ref">{{ section_ref }}</span>.</p>

  <h2 class="section-title">Members of Religious Orders</h2>
  <p>If you are a member of a religious order, you may be exempt from social security and Medicare taxes. You must meet certain requirements to qualify for this exemption.</p>
  <p>If you are a member of a religious order, you must meet the following requirements:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>You must be a member of a religious order.</li>
    <li>You must meet the requirements of the order.</li>
    <li>You must not be subject to SE tax or FICA tax.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="section-title">Taxable Earnings</h2>
  <p>If you are an employee of a church or religious organization, your earnings are generally not subject to SE tax. However, you may be subject to FICA tax.</p>
  <p>If you are a member of a religious order, your earnings may be subject to SE tax and FICA tax, depending on your status.</p>
</div>

