  <h3 class="subsection-title">Table 3. Figuring Nonfarm Net Earnings</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>If your gross income is...</th>
        <th>Then your net earnings are equal to...</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>$2,400 or less</td>
        <td>The greater of:</td>
        <td>The gross income minus your deductible expenses.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>More than $2,400</td>
        <td>The gross income minus your deductible expenses, minus one-half of your self-employment tax.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>For more information on the nonfarm optional method, see <span data-field="section_ref">{{ section_ref }}</span> and Schedule SE (Form 1040).</p>

  <h2 class="section-title">Income Tax: Income and Expenses</h2>
  <p>Some income and expense items are treated differently for tax purposes. For more information, see <span data-field="section_ref">{{ section_ref }}</span>.</p>

  <h3 class="subsection-title">Income Items</h3>
  <p>The tax treatment of offerings and fees, outside contributions, and other income items is discussed here. For more information, see <span data-field="section_ref">{{ section_ref }}</span>.</p>

  <h3 class="subsection-title">Outside Earnings</h3>
  <p>If you are a member of a religious organization and you receive earnings from outside sources, you may be subject to income tax. For more information, see <span data-field="section_ref">{{ section_ref }}</span>.</p>

  <h3 class="subsection-title">Exclusion of Rental Allowance and Fair Rental Value of a Parsonage</h3>
  <p>Ordained, commissioned, or licensed ministers may be entitled to an exclusion of rental allowance and fair rental value of a parsonage. For more information, see <span data-field="section_ref">{{ section_ref }}</span>.</p>
