  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">If your salary is not subject to withholding, or if you are self-employed, you may be able to claim certain deductions or credits.</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">You generally must make estimated tax pay-ments if you expect to owe more than $1,000 in taxes for the year. You must pay estimated taxes if you are self-employed.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Determine your estimated tax by using the IRS Tax Withholding Estimator, available on the IRS website. For Form 1040, use the worksheet in Publication 517. For Form 1040-ES, use the worksheet in Publication 517.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">Retirement Savings Arrangements</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Retirement savings arrangements are plans that allow you to save for retirement on a tax-advantaged basis. You can deduct your contributions to the plan. Your contributions and the earnings on your contributions are not taxed until they are distributed.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Retirement plans for the self-employed. To set up a retirement plan, you must meet certain requirements. You can use a SIMPLE plan, a SIMPLE IRA, or a SEP IRA.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
